    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρεμ-ήρης</span></b> , an Adj. termin., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀραρ-εῖν, ἀραρ-ίσκω</span>, as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμαρής, φρενήρης, χαλκήρης, εὐήρης</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρε- </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρέ-της</span>), as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφήρης,
				ἁλιήρης, τριήρης</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> prob. from (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηρ-</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦρα</span> B) in pr.n. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περιήρης, Διώρης</span> (fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διοήρης</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
